#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186375926 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1292269f-5e99-5354-924d-824238118a8d" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Second-Order ODE When the Right-Hand Side and the Complementary Solution are Dependent"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "709a91f9-3bd0-5c4f-a66f-2ea0764ce03f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=P\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375928} {:answer/id #uuid "93259be1-baa4-59f1-af9a-dd953527dfab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=P{e}^{x}+Qx{e}^{x}-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+6\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375929} {:answer/id #uuid "8754725f-4f38-52c8-8763-34ec1b91f4f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=P\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+6\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375930} {:answer/id #uuid "99677805-7d61-5f03-9ecd-45437093ef7f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=P\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-4x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375931} {:answer/id #uuid "ccdb0818-55e5-53ef-9c44-9e511a4bd37e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=P{e}^{x}+Q{e}^{-x}+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375932}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "99677805-7d61-5f03-9ecd-45437093ef7f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=P\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-4x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375931} :answer-field/id #uuid "4e2c49bb-f39d-51c9-9ff6-7aa714d40224" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375927}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7fccbb6f-7212-518b-a520-56ca0bdcfba4" :question/math-academy-id "q-64276" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+y=8\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x),$ which is the solution to the homogeneous equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+y=0.\n$$\n\nWriting down and solving the auxiliary equation gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+1 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2} & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo $\\lambda =\\pm \\text{i}$, and therefore the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}=P\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\n$$\n\nWe now need to find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x).$\n\nThe particular solution of the inhomogeneous equation cannot be of the form $\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ because this is already included in the complementary function. Therefore, we assume a particular solution of the form\ny_p = x (\\alpha \\cos x + \\beta \\sin x),\n]\nwhere $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $ are constants that are to be determined. \n\nCalculating the first and second derivatives of ${y}_{p}$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p}^{′} & =(\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡x)+x(-\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡x) \\\\ {y}_{p}^{″} & =2(-\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+x(-\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the values of $\\alpha $ and $\\beta ,$ we substitute the derivatives into the differential equation:\n\n$$\n2(-\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+x(-\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡x)+x(\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡x)=8\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\n$$\n\nGrouping the terms on the left-hand side gives\n\n$$\n-2\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡x+2\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡x=8\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2\\beta =0\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡x) \\\\ -2\\alpha =8\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $\\alpha =-4$ and $\\beta =0.$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=-4x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$\n\nThe general solution is given by\n\n$$\ny(x)={y}_{c}(x)+{y}_{p}(x),\n$$\n\nand therefore, the general solution in our case is\n\n$$\ny={y}_{c}+{y}_{p}=P\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-4x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186375933 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6c07e202-40b7-5508-af3d-6a272ed0cbc2" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Initial Value Problem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a83bb3e9-06d7-5b8b-aeb6-3f50c9039c0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2{e}^{2x}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375935} {:answer/id #uuid "1d2980e4-12ba-5840-b8cd-0db87af84cd2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-2{e}^{2x}+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375936} {:answer/id #uuid "cfb1232d-4a9f-587e-84db-5be3b4812db6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{-x}+2{e}^{2x}-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375937} {:answer/id #uuid "104051e3-618f-5207-af59-ae05926f1fc4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{2x}-{e}^{-x}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375938} {:answer/id #uuid "d2f3f98f-c1a4-5c79-8a7d-fc7fd502203d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{-x}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375939}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d2f3f98f-c1a4-5c79-8a7d-fc7fd502203d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{-x}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375939} :answer-field/id #uuid "2bf5a2fe-9230-5ef7-b706-e4640ae5bec9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375934}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "12e0ada2-e53e-5ec1-95a1-f48f0aa38e0b" :question/math-academy-id "q-79633" :question/problem "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-{y}^{′}-2y=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,\\,y(0)=0,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=-1.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x),$ which is the solution to the homogeneous equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-{y}^{′}-2y=0.\n$$\n\nWriting down and solving the auxiliary equation gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda -2 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +1)(\\lambda -2) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo $\\lambda =-1$ or $\\lambda =2$, and therefore the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}(x)=A{e}^{-x}+B{e}^{2x}.\n$$\n\nWe now need to find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x).$\n\nThe right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is $3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$ Therefore, we assume a particular solution of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}=\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡x,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $ are constants that are to be determined. \n\nCalculating the first and second derivatives of ${y}_{p}$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =-\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ {y}^{″} & =-\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the values of $\\alpha $ and $\\beta ,$ we substitute the derivatives into the differential equation:\n\n$$\n-\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡x-(-\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-2(\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡x)=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\n$$\n\nGrouping the terms on the left-hand side gives:\n\n$$\n(-3\\alpha -\\beta )\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+(\\alpha -3\\beta )\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}-3\\alpha -\\beta =3\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡x) \\\\ \\alpha -3\\beta =-1\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $\\alpha =-1,$ $\\beta =0.$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$\n\nThe general solution is given by\n\n$$\ny(x)={y}_{c}(x)+{y}_{p}(x),\n$$\n\nand therefore, the general solution in our case is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{-x}+B{e}^{2x}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$\n\nNow let us find constants $A$ and $B.$ \n\nSubstituting $y(0)=0$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\nA+B-1=0.\n$$\n\nWe now need to apply the condition ${y}^{′}(0)=-1.$ First, we differentiate $y$ to find ${y}^{′}$:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-A{e}^{-x}+2B{e}^{2x}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}(0)=-1$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n-A+2B=-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following system of equations for $A$ and $B$:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}A+B=1 \\\\ -A+2B=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $A=1,$ $B=0.$\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny={e}^{-x}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186375940 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "17b31ef7-a3d0-5315-8dbd-e92eafcce17f" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Second-Order Differential Equation Using Sinusoidal Forcing"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b67c0832-4e76-5390-af76-ae00563b43dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}_{p}=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375942} {:answer/id #uuid "f0493596-3b34-5a6f-8203-5c8e78d4a526" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}_{p}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375943} {:answer/id #uuid "cc149430-3950-5324-9f29-bd01610d3eab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}_{p}=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375944} {:answer/id #uuid "48b102a6-23a1-5f90-8013-6ce3f4ff8713" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}_{p}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375945} {:answer/id #uuid "d31ff34c-1792-52f3-b8d7-94c80c6fa39e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}_{p}=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375946}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d31ff34c-1792-52f3-b8d7-94c80c6fa39e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}_{p}=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375946} :answer-field/id #uuid "40123db5-f61f-5af6-ae44-14c8fafdad97" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375941}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "abf6a408-7e2e-5798-abc8-729a0056824d" :question/math-academy-id "q-93819" :question/problem "Given that the differential equation \n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-4y=8\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\n$$\n\nhas the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x)=A{e}^{-2x}+B{e}^{2x},$ find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ to this equation." :question/worked-solution "The right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is $8\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x.$ So we assume the particular solution of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡2x.\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $ are constants that are to be determined. \n\nCalculating the first and second derivatives of ${y}_{p}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x} & =-2\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+2\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡2x \\\\ \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =-4\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡2x-4\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the values of $\\alpha $ and $\\beta ,$ we substitute the derivatives into the differential equation:\n\n$$\n(-4\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡2x-4\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)-4(\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)=8\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\n$$\n\nGrouping the terms on the left-hand side gives\n\n$$\n-8\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡2x-8\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡2x=8\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x.\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}-8\\alpha =8\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x) \\\\ -8\\beta =0\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $\\alpha =-1,$ $\\beta =0.$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186375947 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1292269f-5e99-5354-924d-824238118a8d" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Second-Order ODE When the Right-Hand Side and the Complementary Solution are Dependent"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c17c96f-5267-5a18-8a9e-2a9b25a4417f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}_{p}=x\\operatorname{cos}⁡6x-x\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375949} {:answer/id #uuid "bab9372f-b941-5692-87b2-f0a04abc04a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}_{p}=-x\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375950} {:answer/id #uuid "507a9994-fc2d-5559-9c94-4c02fa21ca26" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}_{p}=x\\operatorname{cos}⁡6x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375951} {:answer/id #uuid "262f36f4-6d8b-5226-9c8f-1b486cdebe62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}_{p}=-3x\\operatorname{cos}⁡6x+x\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375952} {:answer/id #uuid "a9e9e07f-2e24-5007-87eb-695a26a7ab46" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}_{p}=2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡6x+5x\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375953}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bab9372f-b941-5692-87b2-f0a04abc04a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}_{p}=-x\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375950} :answer-field/id #uuid "5823a07a-88de-56a4-8802-370c975bd0e4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375948}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c05c30a6-28a6-5452-ac44-e10a5f53cc02" :question/math-academy-id "q-93824" :question/problem "Given that the differential equation \n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+36y=-12\\operatorname{cos}⁡6x\n$$\n\nhas the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x)=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡6x+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x,$ find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ to this equation." :question/worked-solution "The particular solution of the inhomogeneous equation cannot be of the form $\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡6x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡6x$ because this is already included in the complementary function. Therefore, we assume a particular solution of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}=x(\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡6x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡6x),\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $ are constants that are to be determined. \n\nCalculating the first and second derivatives of ${y}_{p}$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x} & =(\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡6x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡6x)+6x(-\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡6x+\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡6x) \\\\ \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =12(-\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡6x+\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡6x)-36x(\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡6x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡6x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the values of $\\alpha $ and $\\beta ,$ we substitute the derivatives into the differential equation:\n\n$$\n12(-\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡6x+\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡6x)-36x(\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡6x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡6x)+36x(\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡6x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡6x)=-12\\operatorname{cos}⁡6x\n$$\n\nGrouping the terms on the left-hand side gives\n\n$$\n-12\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡6x+12\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡6x=-12\\operatorname{cos}⁡6x.\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}12\\beta =-12\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡6x) \\\\ -12\\alpha =0\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x)\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $\\alpha =0$ and $\\beta =-1.$ Therefore, the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=-x\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186375954 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6c07e202-40b7-5508-af3d-6a272ed0cbc2" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Initial Value Problem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "408ba523-7def-5279-8ae0-6539d85fd34f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{2x}-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375956} {:answer/id #uuid "fc25a5b0-95db-5687-8baa-488a7c2257aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-3{e}^{x}-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375957} {:answer/id #uuid "bf99f4a8-bd09-5665-866b-07d99c168a83" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=5{e}^{x}-{e}^{2x}-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375958} {:answer/id #uuid "6adb4503-118b-5805-a502-4badc060f9a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=6{e}^{2x}-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375959} {:answer/id #uuid "618c7793-c5c7-57b4-b4e9-4e7ccf74f126" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2{e}^{x}+2{e}^{2x}-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375960}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "618c7793-c5c7-57b4-b4e9-4e7ccf74f126" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2{e}^{x}+2{e}^{2x}-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375960} :answer-field/id #uuid "e254fa8b-02dd-5219-943f-1b8e9741c4ab" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375955}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "aa611cc8-a42d-54e7-b968-c63b5188a4e5" :question/math-academy-id "q-93834" :question/problem "Given that the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-3\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2y=20\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\n$$\n\nhas the general solution\n\n$$\ny(x)=A{e}^{x}+B{e}^{2x}-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x,\n$$\n\nsolve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-3\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2y=20\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x,\\,y(0)=3,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We find the constants $A$ and $B$ by substituting the initial conditions.\n\n- Substituting $y(0)=3$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3 & =A{e}^{0}+B{e}^{2(0)}-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2(0)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2(0) \\\\ 3 & =A+B-1 \\\\ 4 & =A+B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Differentiating $y$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=A{e}^{x}+2B{e}^{2x}-6\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x.\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}(0)=0$ into the derivative gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0 & =A{e}^{0}+2B{e}^{2(0)}-6\\operatorname{cos}⁡2(0)+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2(0) \\\\ 0 & =A+2B-6 \\\\ 6 & =A+2B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following system of equations for $A$ and $B:$\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}A+B=4 \\\\ A+2B=6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $A=2,B=2.$\n\nFinally, since $A=2$ and $B=2,$ we have the following solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\ny=2{e}^{x}+2{e}^{2x}-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\n$$"}]}
